description:
Hi,

In experimental packages growing more mature, I end up with many functions being simply renamed.

This causes many functions to be just a call to `deprecate_warn()` and then a call to the replacement function. I think it would be clearer if there was a purrr-style adverb to be used.

Something like this:


``` r
deprecatedly = function(f, what, when, with=rlang::caller_arg(f), details=NULL, type="warn"){
  if(!stringr::str_ends(with, "\\(\\)")) with=paste0(with,"()")
  if(!stringr::str_ends(what, "\\(\\)")) what=paste0(what,"()")
  function(...){
    lifecycle::deprecate_warn(when, what, with, details)
    f(...)
  }
}

new_function = function(){
  "foo"
}

old_function = deprecatedly(new_function, what="old_function", when="0.1")

old_function()
#> Warning: `old_function()` was deprecated in <NA> 0.1.
#> ℹ Please use `new_function()` instead.
#> This warning is displayed once every 8 hours.
#> Call `lifecycle::last_lifecycle_warnings()` to see where this warning was
#> generated.
#> [1] "foo"
```

<sup>Created on 2024-12-26 with [reprex v2.1.1](https://reprex.tidyverse.org)</sup>

As it is used for superseded functions this isn't very nice.

```r
f <- function() {
  lifecycle::signal_stage("superseded", "recode()", "case_match()")
}

for (i in 1:1000) {
  f()
}
```

<img width="856" alt="image" src="https://github.com/r-lib/lifecycle/assets/18258854/4f285adb-14d0-41d9-b718-f59e8719a0e3">

E.g. this made `dplyr::recode()` so much slower than before.

This test in the admiral package fails when run in from revdepcheck, but not when run locally:

```R
test_that("derive_var_agegr_fda Test 1: A warning is issued if `derive_var_agegr_fda()` is called", { # nolint
  with_options(lifecycle_verbosity = "warning", {
    expect_warning(
      derive_var_agegr_fda(admiral_dm, age_var = AGE, new_var = AGEGR1),
      "deprecated",
      fixed = TRUE
    )
  })
})
```

Presumably because of the on CRAN check, which should only be used in `deprecate_soft()`?

All of the images for lifecycle in my package are broken.  They used to work and stopped some time ago, not sure exactly when.

I have re-run `usethis::use_lifecycle()` and ensured that the svg files are in man/figures.

Here is an example of one rendered help document, documenation code above the function in the .R file,  and the  .Rd file:

